{
  "title": "27: al-Naml النمل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰسٓ‌ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْقُرْاٰنِ وَكِتَابٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(1)\nTAA SIN! TILKA AAYAATUL QURAANE WA KETAABIM MOBEEN\nTa, Seen. These are the signs of the Quran and a manifest Book,\nهُدًى وَّبُشْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(2)\nHODANW WA BUSHRAA LIL-MOMENEENAL\na guidance and good news for the faithful\nالَّذِيْنَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَ هُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(3)\nLAZEENA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM YOOQENOON\n—those who maintain the prayer and pay the zakat, and who are certain of the Hereafter.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ زَيَّنَّا لَهُمْ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَهُمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَؕ‏(4)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-AAKHERATE ZAYYANNAA LAHUM A-A’MAALAHUM FAHUM YA’MAHOON\nAs for those who do not believe in the Hereafter, We have made their deeds seem decorous to them, and so they are bewildered.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَهُمْ سُوْٓءُ الْعَذَابِ وَهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ هُمُ الْاَخْسَرُوْنَ‏(5)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA LAHUM SOOO-UL A’ZAABE WA HUM FIL AAKHERATE HOMUL AKHSAROON\nThey are the ones for whom there is a terrible punishment, and they are the ones who will be the biggest losers in the Hereafter.\nوَاِنَّكَ لَتُلَقَّى الْقُرْاٰنَ مِنْ لَّدُنْ حَكِيْمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(6)\nWA INNAKA LATOLAQQAL QURAANA MIL LADUN HAKEEMIN A’LEEM\nIndeed you receive the Quran from One who is all-wise, all-knowing.\nاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَهْلِهٖۤ اِنِّىْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًاؕ سَاٰتِيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ اَوْ اٰتِيْكُمْ بِشِهَابٍ قَبَسٍ لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُوْنَ‏(7)\nIZ QAALA MOOSAA LE-AHLIHI INNEE AANASTO NAARAN, SA-AATEEKUM MINHAA BEKHABARIN AW AATEEKUM BESHEHAABIN QABASIL LA-A’LLAKUM TASTALOON\nWhen Moses said to his family, ‘Indeed I descry a fire! I will bring you some news from it, or bring you a firebrand so that you may warm yourselves.’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهَا نُوْدِىَ اَنْۢ بُوْرِكَ مَنْ فِى النَّارِ وَ مَنْ حَوْلَهَا ؕ وَسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(8)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHAA NOODEYA AM BOOREKA MAN FIN NAARE WA MAN HAWLAHAA, WA SUBHAANAL LAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN\nWhen he came to it, he was called: ‘Blessed is He who is in the fire and who is [as well] around it, and immaculate is Allah, the Lord of all the worlds!’\nيٰمُوْسٰۤى اِنَّهٗۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُۙ‏(9)\nYAA MOOSAA INNAHU ANAL LAAHUL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEMO\n‘O Moses! Indeed I am Allah, the All-mighty, the All-wise.’\nوَاَ لْقِ عَصَاكَ‌ ؕ فَلَمَّا رَاٰهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَاَنَّهَا جَآنٌّ وَّلّٰى مُدْبِرًا وَّلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ‌ ؕ يٰمُوْسٰى لَا تَخَفْ اِنِّىْ لَا يَخَافُ لَدَىَّ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ ‌ۖ‏(10)\nWA ALQE A’SAAKA, FALAMMAA RA-AAHAA TAHTAZZO KA-ANNAHAA JAAANNUW WALLAA MUDBERAWN WA LAM YO-A’QQIB, YAA MOOSAA LAA TAKHAF, INNEE LAA YAKHAAFO LADAYYAL MURSALOON.\n‘Throw down your staff!’ When he saw it wriggling, as if it were a snake, he turned his back [to flee], without looking back. ‘O Moses! ‘Do not be afraid. Indeed the apostles are not afraid before Me,\nاِلَّا مَنْ ظَلَمَ ثُمَّ بَدَّلَ حُسْنًۢا بَعْدَ سُوْٓءٍ فَاِنِّىْ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(11)\nILLAA MAN ZALAMA SUMMA BADDALA HUSNAM BA’DA SOOO-IN FA-INNEE GHAFOORUR RAHEEMUN\nnor those who do wrong and then make up for [their] fault with goodness, for indeed I am all-forgiving, all-merciful.’\nوَاَدْخِلْ يَدَكَ فِىْ جَيْبِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَآءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوْٓءٍ‌ فِىْ تِسْعِ اٰيٰتٍ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَقَوْمِهٖؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(12)\nWA ADKHIL YADAKA FEE JAYBEKA TAKHRUJ BAYZAAA-A MIN GHAIRE SOOO-IN, FEE TIS-E’ AAYAATIN ELAA FIRA’WNA WA QAWMEHI, INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\n‘Insert your hand into your shirt. It will emerge white and bright, without any fault—among nine signs meant for Pharaoh and his people. Indeed they are a transgressing lot.’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتْهُمْ اٰيٰتُنَا مُبْصِرَةً قَالُوْا هٰذَا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(13)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM AAYAATONAA MUBSERATAN QAALOO HAAZAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nBut when Our signs came to them, as eye-openers, they said, ‘This is plain magic.’\nوَجَحَدُوْا بِهَا وَاسْتَيْقَنَتْهَاۤ اَنْفُسُهُمْ ظُلْمًا وَّعُلُوًّا‌ ؕ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(14)\nWA JAHADOO BEHAA WASTAYQANATHAA ANFOSOHUM ZULMAWN WA O’LUWWAA, FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUFSEDEEN.\nThey impugned them, wrongfully and out of arrogance, though they were convinced in their hearts [of their veracity]. So observe how the fate of the agents of corruption was!\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ وَ سُلَيْمٰنَ عِلْمًا‌ ۚ وَقَالَا الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ فَضَّلَنَا عَلٰى كَثِيْرٍ مِّنْ عِبَادِهِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(15)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA DAAWOODA WA SOLAYMAANA I’LMAN, WA QAALAL HAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE FAZZALANAA A’LAA KASEERIM MIN E’BAADEHIL MOAMENEEN.\nCertainly, We gave knowledge to David and Solomon, and they said, ‘All praise belongs to Allah, who granted us an advantage over many of His faithful servants.’\nوَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمٰنُ دَاوٗدَ‌ وَقَالَ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ عُلِّمْنَا مَنْطِقَ الطَّيْرِ وَاُوْتِيْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍؕ‌ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْفَضْلُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(16)\nWA WARESA SULAYMAANO DAAWOODA WA QAALA YAA AYYOHAN NAASO U’LLIMNAA MANTEQAT TAYRE WA OOTEENAA MIN KULLE SHAYIN, INNA HAAZAA LAHOWAL FAZLUL MOBEEN\nSolomon inherited from David, and he said, ‘O people! We have been taught the speech of the birds, and we have been given out of everything. Indeed this is a manifest advantage.’\nوَحُشِرَ لِسُلَيْمٰنَ جُنُوْدُهٗ مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ وَالطَّيْرِ فَهُمْ يُوْزَعُوْنَ‏(17)\nWA HOSHERA LESOLAYMAANA JONOODOHU MENAL JINNE WAL INSE WAT-TAYRE FAHUM YOOZA-O’ON\n[Once] Solomon’s hosts were marched out for him, comprising jinn, humans and birds, and they were held in check.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَاۤ اَتَوْا عَلٰى وَادِ النَّمْلِۙ قَالَتْ نَمْلَةٌ يّٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّمْلُ ادْخُلُوْا مَسٰكِنَكُمْ‌ۚ لَا يَحْطِمَنَّكُمْ سُلَيْمٰنُ وَجُنُوْدُهٗۙ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(18)\nHAATAA EZAA ATAW A’LAA WAADIN NAMLE, QAALAT NAMLATUYN YAA AYYOHAN NAMLUD KHOLOO MASAAKENAKUM, LAA YAHTEMANNAKUM SOLAYMAANO WA JONOODOHU, WA HUM LAA YASHO’ROON.\nWhen they came to the Valley of Ants, an ant said, ‘O ants! Enter your dwellings, lest Solomon and his hosts should trample on you while they are unaware.’\nفَتَبَسَّمَ ضَاحِكًا مِّنْ قَوْلِهَا وَقَالَ رَبِّ اَوْزِعْنِىْۤ اَنْ اَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ الَّتِىْۤ اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ وَعَلٰى وَالِدَىَّ وَاَنْ اَعْمَلَ صَالِحًا تَرْضٰٮهُ وَاَدْخِلْنِىْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ فِىْ عِبَادِكَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(19)\nFATABASSAMA ZAAHEKAM MIN QAWLEHAA WA QAALA RABBE AWZE’NEE AN ASHKORA NE’MATAKAL LATEE ANA’MTA A’LAYYA WA A’LAA WAALEDAYYA WA AN A-A’MALA SAALEHAN TARZAAHO WA ADKHILNEE BERAHMATEKA FEE E’BAADEKAS SAALEHEEN.\nWhereat he smiled, amused at its words, and he said, ‘My Lord! Inspire me to give thanks for Your blessing with which You have blessed me and my parents, and that I may do righteous deeds which please You, and admit me, by Your mercy, among Your righteous servants.’\nوَتَفَقَّدَ الطَّيْرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِىَ لَاۤ اَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ ‌ۖ  اَمْ كَانَ مِنَ الْغَآئِبِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA TAFAQQADAT TAYRA FAQAALA MAA LEYA LAA ARAL HUDHODA, AM KAANA MENAL GHAAEBEEN.\n[One day] he reviewed the birds, and said, ‘Why do I not see the hoopoe? Or is he absent?’\nلَاُعَذِّبَنَّهٗ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا اَوْ لَا۟اَذْبَحَنَّهٗۤ اَوْ لَيَاْتِيَنِّىْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(21)\nLA-O-A’ZZEBANNAHU A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAN AWLAA AZBAHANNAHU AWLAYAATEYANNEE BESULTANIM MOBEEN.\n‘I will punish him with a severe punishment, or I will behead him, unless he brings me a credible excuse.’\nفَمَكَثَ غَيْرَ بَعِيْدٍ فَقَالَ اَحَطْتُّ بِمَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهٖ وَ جِئْتُكَ مِنْ سَبَاٍۢ بِنَبَاٍ يَّقِيْنٍ‏(22)\nFAMAKASA GHAYRO BA-E’EDIN FAQAALA AHATTO BEMAA LAM TOHIT BEHI WA JE’TOKA MIN SABA-IM BENABAIYN YAQEEN\nHe did not stay for long [before he turned up] and said, ‘I have alighted on something which you have not alighted on, and I have brought you from Sheba a definite report.\nاِنِّىْ وَجَدتُّ امْرَاَةً تَمْلِكُهُمْ وَاُوْتِيَتْ مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(23)\nINNEE WAJADTUM RA-ATAN TAMLEKOHUM WA OOTEYAT MIN KULLE SHAY-IWN WA LAHAA A’RSHUN A’ZEEM.\nI found a woman ruling over them, and she has been given everything, and she has a great throne.\nوَجَدْتُّهَا وَقَوْمَهَا يَسْجُدُوْنَ لِلشَّمْسِ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ فَهُمْ لَا يَهْتَدُوْنَۙ‏(24)\nWA JADTOHAA WA QAWMAHAA YASJODOONA LISH-SHAMSE MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA ZAYYANA LAHOMUSH SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM FASADDATHUM A’NIS SABEELE FAHUM LAA YAHTADOON.\nI found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allah, and Satan has made their deeds seem decorous to them—thus he has barred them from the way [of Allah], so they are not guided—\nاَلَّا يَسْجُدُوْا لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ يُخْرِجُ الْخَبْءَ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُخْفُوْنَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(25)\nALLAAYASJODOO LILLAAHIL LAAZEE YUKHREJUL KHAB-A FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZE WA YA’LAMO MA TUKHFOONA WA MAA TO’LENOON.\nso that they do not prostrate themselves to Allah, who brings forth the hidden in the heavens and the earth, and He knows whatever you hide and whatever you disclose.\nاَللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ ۩‏(26)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL A’ZEEM\nAllah—there is no god except Him—is the Lord of the Great Throne.’\nقَالَ سَنَنْظُرُ اَصَدَقْتَ اَمْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(27)\nQAALA SANANZORO A-SADAQTA AM KUNTA MENAL KAAZEBEEN\nHe said, ‘We shall see whether you are truthful, or if you are one of the liars.\nاِذْهَبْ بِّكِتٰبِىْ هٰذَا فَاَلْقِهْ اِلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(28)\nIZHAB BEKETAABEE HAAZAA FA-ALQEH ELAYHIM SUMMA TAWALLA A’NHUM FANZUR MAA ZAA YARJE-O’ON\nTake this letter of mine and deliver it to them. Then draw away from them and observe what [response] they return.’\nقَالَتْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَؤُا اِنِّىْۤ اُلْقِىَ اِلَىَّ كِتٰبٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(29)\nQAALAT YAA-AYYOHAL MALA-O INNEE ULQEYA ELAYYA KETAABUN KAREEM.\nShe said, ‘O [members of the] elite! Indeed a noble letter has been delivered to me.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ سُلَيْمٰنَ وَاِنَّهٗ بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِۙ‏(30)\nINNAHU MEN SOLAYMAANA WA INNAHU BISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM.\nIt is from Solomon, and it begins in the name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful.\nاَلَّا تَعْلُوْا عَلَىَّ وَاْتُوْنِىْ مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nALLAA TA’LOO A’LAYYA WAATOONEE MUSLEMEEN.\n[It states,] ‘‘Do not defy me, and come to me in submission.’’ ’\nقَالَتْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَؤُا اَفْتُوْنِىْ فِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ‌ۚ مَا كُنْتُ قَاطِعَةً اَمْرًا حَتّٰى تَشْهَدُوْنِ‏(32)\nQAALAT YAA AYYOHAL MALAO AFTOONEE FEE AMREE, MAA KUNTO QAATE-A’TAN AMRAN HATTAA TASH-HADOON\nShe said, ‘O [members of the] elite! Give me your opinion concerning my matter. I do not decide any matter until you are present.’\nقَالُوْا نَحْنُ اُولُوْا قُوَّةٍ وَّاُولُوْا بَاْسٍ شَدِيْدٍ ۙ وَّالْاَمْرُ اِلَيْكِ فَانْظُرِىْ مَاذَا تَاْمُرِيْنَ‏(33)\nQAALOO NAHNO OOLOO QUWWATIWN WA OOLOO BAA-SIN SHADEED, WAL AMRO ELAYKA FANZUR MAA ZAA TAAMOREEN.\nThey said, ‘We are powerful and possess a great might. But it is up to you to command. So consider what orders you will give.’\nقَالَتْ اِنَّ الْمُلُوْكَ اِذَا دَخَلُوْا قَرْيَةً اَفْسَدُوْهَا وَجَعَلُوْۤا اَعِزَّةَ اَهْلِهَاۤ اَذِلَّةً  ‌ۚ وَكَذٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(34)\nQAALAT INNAL MOLOOKA IZAA DAKHALOO QARYATAN AFSADOOHAA WA JA-A’LOO A-I’ZZATA AHLEHAA AZILLATAH, WA KAZAALEKA YAF-A’LOON.\nShe said, ‘Indeed when kings enter a town, they devastate it, and make the mightiest of its people the weakest. That is how they act.\nوَاِنِّىْ مُرْسِلَةٌ اِلَيْهِمْ بِهَدِيَّةٍ فَنٰظِرَةٌۢ بِمَ يَرْجِعُ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(35)\nWA INNEE MURSELATUN ELAYHIM BEHADIYYATIN FANAAZERATUM BEMA YARJE-O’L MURSALOON.\nI will send them a gift, and see what the envoys bring back.’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ سُلَيْمٰنَ قَالَ اَتُمِدُّوْنَنِ بِمَالٍ فَمَاۤ اٰتٰٮنِۦَ اللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّاۤ اٰتٰٮكُمْ‌ۚ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ بِهَدِيَّتِكُمْ تَفْرَحُوْنَ‏(36)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A SULAYMAANA QAALA ATOMIDDOONANE BEMAALIN, FAMAA AATAANEYAL LAAHO KHAYRUM MIMMAA AATAAKUM, BAL ANTUM BEHADIYYATEKUM TAFRAHOON.\nSo when he came to Solomon, he said, ‘Are you aiding me with wealth? What Allah has given me is better than what He has given you. Indeed, you are proud of your gift!\nاِرْجِعْ اِلَيْهِمْ فَلَنَاْتِيَنَّهُمْ بِجُنُوْدٍ لَّا قِبَلَ لَهُمْ بِهَا وَلَنُخْرِجَنَّهُمْ مِّنْهَاۤ اَذِلَّةً وَّهُمْ صٰغِرُوْنَ‏(37)\nIRJE’ ELAYHIM FALANAATEYANNAHUM BEJONOODIL LAA QEBALA LAHUM BEHAA WA LANUKHREJANNAHUM MINHAA AZILLATAWAN WA HUM SAAGHEROON.\nGo back to them, for we will come at them with hosts which they cannot face, and we will expel them from it, abased and degraded.’\nقَالَ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَؤُا اَيُّكُمْ يَاْتِيْنِىْ بِعَرْشِهَا قَبْلَ اَنْ يَّاْتُوْنِىْ مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(38)\nQAALA YAA-AYYOHAL MALA-O AYYOKUM YAATEENEE BE-A’RSHEHAA QABLA AYN YAATOONEE MUSLEMEEN.\nHe said, ‘O [members of the] elite! Which of you will bring me her throne before they come to me in submission?’\nقَالَ عِفْرِيْتٌ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ اَنَا اٰتِيْكَ بِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ تَقُوْمَ مِنْ مَّقَامِكَ‌ۚ وَاِنِّىْ عَلَيْهِ لَقَوِىٌّ اَمِيْنٌ‏(39)\nQAALA I’FREETUM MENAL JINNE ANAA AATEEKA BEHI QABLA AN TAQOOMA MIM MAQAAMEK, WA INNEE A’LAYHE LAQAWIYYUN AMEEN.\nAn afreet from among the jinn said, ‘I will bring it to you before you rise from your place. I have the power to do it and am trustworthy.’\nقَالَ الَّذِىْ عِنْدَهٗ عِلْمٌ مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ اَنَا اٰتِيْكَ بِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ يَّرْتَدَّ اِلَيْكَ طَرْفُكَ‌ؕ فَلَمَّا رَاٰهُ مُسْتَقِرًّا عِنْدَهٗ قَالَ هٰذَا مِنْ فَضْلِ رَبِّىْ‌ۖ لِيَبْلُوَنِىْٓ ءَاَشْكُرُ اَمْ اَكْفُرُ‌ؕ وَمَنْ شَكَرَ فَاِنَّمَا يَشْكُرُ لِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاِنَّ رَبِّىْ غَنِىٌّ كَرِيْمٌ‏(40)\nQAALAL LAZEE I’NDAHU I’LMUM MENAL KETAABE ANAA AATEEKA BEHI QABLA AYN YARTADDA ELAYKA TARFOK, FALAMMAA RA-AAHO MUSTAQIRRAN I’NDAHU QAALAA HAAZAA MIN FAZLE RABBEE, LEYABLOWANEE, A-ASHKORO AM AKFOR, WA MAN SHAKARA FA-INNAMAA YASHKORO LENAFSEHI, WA MAN KAFARA FA-INNA RABBEE GHANIYYUN KAREEM.\nThe one who had knowledge of the Book said, ‘I will bring it to you in the twinkling of an eye.’ So when he saw it set near him, he said, ‘This is by the grace of my Lord, to test me if I will give thanks or be ungrateful. Whoever gives thanks, gives thanks only for his own sake. And whoever is ungrateful [should know that] my Lord is indeed all-sufficient, all-generous.’\nقَالَ نَكِّرُوْا لَهَا عَرْشَهَا نَنْظُرْ اَتَهْتَدِىْۤ اَمْ تَكُوْنُ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(41)\nQAALA NAKKEROO LAHAA A’RSHAHAA NANZOR ATAHTADEE AM TAKOONO MENAL LAZEENA LAA YAHTADOON.\nHe said, ‘Disguise her throne for her, so that we may see whether she is discerning or if she is one of the undiscerning ones.’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ قِيْلَ اَهٰكَذَا عَرْشُكِ‌ؕ قَالَتْ كَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ‌ۚ وَاُوْتِيْنَا الْعِلْمَ مِنْ قَبْلِهَا وَ كُنَّا مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(42)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AT QEELA A-HAAKAZAA A’RSHOK, QAALAT KA-ANNAHU HOO, WA OOTEENAL I’LMA MIN QABLEHAA WA KUNNAA MUSLEMEEN.\nSo when she came, it was said [to her], ‘Is your throne like this one?’ She said, ‘It seems to be the same, and we were informed before it, and we had submitted.’\nوَصَدَّهَا مَا كَانَتْ تَّعْبُدُ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّهَا كَانَتْ مِنْ قَوْمٍ كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(43)\nWA SADDAHAA MAA KAANAT TA’BODO MIN DOONIL LAAH, INNAHAA QAANAT MIN QAWMIN KAAFEREEN.\nShe had been barred [from the way of Allah] by what she used to worship besides Allah, for she belonged to a faithless people.\nقِيْلَ لَهَا ادْخُلِى الصَّرْحَ‌ ۚ فَلَمَّا رَاَتْهُ حَسِبَتْهُ لُجَّةً وَّكَشَفَتْ عَنْ سَاقَيْهَا ‌ؕ قَالَ اِنَّهٗ صَرْحٌ مُّمَرَّدٌ مِّنْ قَوَارِيْرَ ۙ‌قَالَتْ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِىْ وَ اَسْلَمْتُ مَعَ سُلَيْمٰنَ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(44)\nQEELA LAHAD KHOLIS SARH, FALAMMAA RA-ATHO HASEBATHO LUJJATAWN WA KASHAFAT A’N SAAQAYHAA, QAALA INNAHU SARHUM MOMARRADUM MIN QAWAAREER, QAALAT RABBE INNEE ZALAMTO NAFSEE WA ASLAMTO MA-A’ SOLAYMAANA LILLAAHE RABBIL A-A’LAMEEN.\nIt was said to her, ‘Enter the palace.’ So when she saw it, she supposed it to be a pool of water, and she bared her shanks. He said, ‘It is a palace paved with crystal.’ She said, ‘My Lord! Indeed I have wronged myself, and I submit with Solomon to Allah, the Lord of all the worlds.’\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلٰى ثَمُوْدَ اَخَاهُمْ صٰلِحًا اَنِ اعْبُدُوْا اللّٰهَ فَاِذَا هُمْ فَرِيْقٰنِ يَخْتَصِمُوْنَ‏(45)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ELAA SAMOODA AKHAAHUM SAALEHAN ANE’BODUL LAALA FA-IZAA HUM FAREEQAANE YAKHTASEMOON.\nCertainly We sent to Thamud Salih, their brother, [with the summons:] ‘Worship Allah!’ But thereat they became two groups contending with each other.\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لِمَ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ قَبْلَ الْحَسَنَةِ‌‌ۚ لَوْلَا تَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ اللّٰهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(46)\nQAALA YAA QAWME LEMA TAS-TA’JELOONA BIS-SAYYEATE QABLAL HASANATE, LAWLAA TASTAGHFEROONAL LAAHA LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nHe said, ‘O My people! Why do you press for evil sooner than for good? Why do you not plead to Allah for forgiveness so that you may receive His mercy?’\nقَالُوا اطَّيَّرْنَا بِكَ وَبِمَنْ مَّعَكَ‌ ؕ قَالَ طٰٓئِرُكُمْ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ‌ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(47)\nQAALUT TAYYARNAA BEKA WA BEMAM MA-A’K, QAALA TAAA-EROKUM I’NDAL LAAHE BAL ANTUM QAWMUN TUFTANOON.\nThey said, ‘We take you and those who are with you for a bad omen.’ He said, ‘Your bad omens are from Allah. Indeed, you are a people being tested.’\nوَكَانَ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ تِسْعَةُ رَهْطٍ يُّفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا يُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA KAANA FIL MADEENATE TIS-A’TO RAHTIYN YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE WA LAA YUSLEHOON.\nThere were nine persons in the city who caused corruption in the land and did not set things right.\nقَالُوْا تَقَاسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ لَنُبَيِّتَنَّهٗ وَ اَهْلَهٗ ثُمَّ لَنَقُوْلَنَّ لِوَلِيِّهٖ مَا شَهِدْنَا مَهْلِكَ اَهْلِهٖ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(49)\nQAALOO TAQAASAMOO BILLAAHE LANOFAYYETANNAHU WA AHLAHU SUMMA LANAQOOLANNA LEWALIYYEHI MAA SHAHIDNAA MAHLEKA AHLEHI WA INNAA LASAADEQOON.\nThey said, ‘Swear by Allah that we will attack him and his family by night. Then we will tell his heir that we were not present at the murder of his family and that we speak the truth.’\nوَمَكَرُوْا مَكْرًا وَّمَكَرْنَا مَكْرًا وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA MAKAROO MAKRAWN WA MAKARNAA MAKRAWN WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON\nThey devised a plot, and We [too] devised a plan, but they were not aware.\nفَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ مَكْرِهِمْۙ اَنَّا دَمَّرْنٰهُمْ وَقَوْمَهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(51)\nFANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATO MAKREHIM, ANNAA DAMMARNAAHUM WA QAWMAHUM AJMA-E’EN.\nSo observe how was the outcome of their plotting, as We destroyed them and all their people.\nفَتِلْكَ بُيُوْتُهُمْ خَاوِيَةً ۢ بِمَا ظَلَمُوْا‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(52)\nFATILKA BOYOOTOHUM KHAAWEYATAM BEMAA ZALAMOO, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMIYN YA’LAMOON.\nSo there lay their houses, fallen in ruin because of their wrongdoing. There is indeed a sign in that for a people who have knowledge.\nوَاَنْجَيْنَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَكَانُوْا يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(53)\nWA ANJAYNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA KAANOO YATTAQOON.\nAnd We delivered those who had faith and were Godwary.\nوَلُوْطًا اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَتَاْتُوْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ وَاَنْتُمْ تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(54)\nWA LOOTAN IZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI ATAATOONAL FAAHESHATA WA ANTUM TUBSERAOON.\n[We also sent] Lot, when he said to his people, ‘What! Do you commit this indecency while you look on?\nاَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الرِّجَالَ شَهْوَةً مِّنْ دُوْنِ النِّسَآءِ‌ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(55)\nA-INNAKUM LATAATOO NAR REJAALA SHAHWATAM MIN DOONIN NESAAA, BAL ANTUM QAWMUN TAJHALOON.\nDo you approach men with [sexual] desire instead of women?! Indeed, you are a senseless lot!’\nفَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اَخْرِجُوْۤا اٰلَ لُوْطٍ مِّنْ قَرْيَتِكُمْ‌ۚ اِنَّهُمْ اُنَاسٌ يَّتَطَهَّرُوْنَ‏(56)\nFAMAA KAANA JAWAABA QAWMEHI ILLAA AN QAALOO AKHREJOO AALA LOOTIM MIN QARYATEKUM, INNAHUM ONAASUYN YATATAHHAROON.\nBut the only answer of his people was that they said, ‘Expel Lot’s family from your town! They are indeed a puritanical lot.’\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَ اَهْلَهٗۤ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ قَدَّرْنٰهَا مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(57)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WA AHLAHU ILLAM RA-ATAHU, QADDARNAAHAA MENAL GHAABEREEN.\nSo We delivered him and his family, except his wife. We ordained her to be among those who remained behind.\nوَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّطَرًا‌ۚ فَسَآءَ مَطَرُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(58)\n58: WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHIM MATARAA, FA-SAAA-A MATARUL MUNZEREEN.\nThen We poured down upon them a rain [of stones]. Evil was that rain for those who had been warned!\nقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى عِبَادِهِ الَّذِيْنَ اصْطَفٰىؕ ءٰۤللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ اَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَؕ‏(59)\nQOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHE WA SALAAMUN A’LAA E’BAADEHIL LAZEENAS TAFAA, AALLAAHO KHAYRUN AMMAA YUSHREKOON.\nSay, ‘All praise belongs to Allah, and Peace be to the servants whom He has chosen.’ Is Allah better, or the partners they ascribe [to Him]?\nاَمَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَاَنْزَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً‌ ۚ فَاَنْۢبَتْنَا بِهٖ حَدَآئِقَ ذَاتَ بَهْجَةٍ‌ ۚ مَا كَانَ لَكُمْ اَنْ تُنْۢبِتُوْا شَجَرَهَا ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ يَّعْدِلُوْنَ ؕ‏(60)\nAMMAN KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA ANZALA LAKUM MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-A, FA-AMBATNAA BEHI HADAAA-EQA ZAATA BAHJAH, MAA KAANA LAKUM AN TUMBETOO SHAJARAHAA, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, BAL HUM QAUMUYN YA’DELOON.\nIs He who created the heavens and the earth, and sends down for you water from the sky, whereby We grow delightful gardens, whose trees you could never cause to grow...? What! Is there a god besides Allah? Indeed, they are a lot who equate [others with Allah].\nاَمَّنْ جَعَلَ الْاَرْضَ قَرَارًا وَّجَعَلَ خِلٰلَهَاۤ اَنْهٰرًا وَّجَعَلَ لَهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ حَاجِزًا‌ ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ ؕ‏(61)\nAMMAN JA-A’LAL ARZA QARAARAWN WA JA-A’LA KHELAALAHAA ANHAARAWN WA JA-A’LA LAHAA RAWAASEYA WA JA-A’LA BAYNAL BAHRAYNE HAAJEZAA, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nIs He who made the earth an abode [for you], and made rivers [flowing] through it, and set firm mountains for it [’s stability], and set a barrier between the two seas...? What! Is there a god besides Allah? Indeed, most of them do not know.\nاَمَّنْ يُّجِيْبُ الْمُضْطَرَّ اِذَا دَعَاهُ وَيَكْشِفُ السُّوْٓءَ وَيَجْعَلُكُمْ خُلَفَآءَ الْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ ‌ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ ؕ‏(62)\nAMMAYN YOJEEBUL MUZTARRA EZAA DA-A’AHO WA YAKSHEFUS SOOO-A WA YAJ-A’LOKUM KHOLAFAAA-AL ARZ, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, QALEELAM MAA TAZAKKAROON.\nIs He who answers the call of the distressed [person] when he invokes Him and removes his distress, and makes you successors on the earth...? What! Is there a god besides Allah? Little is the admonition that you take.\nاَمَّنْ يَّهْدِيْكُمْ فِىْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْبَرِّ وَ الْبَحْرِ وَمَنْ يُّرْسِلُ الرِّيٰحَ بُشْرًۢا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَحْمَتِهٖؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ تَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَؕ‏(63)\nAMMAYN YAHDEEKUM FEE ZOLOMAATIL BARRE WAL BAHRE WA MAYN YURSELUR REYAAHA BUSHRAM BAYNA YADAY RAHMATEH, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, TA-A’ALAL LAAHO A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nIs He who guides you in the darkness of land and sea and who sends the winds as harbingers of His mercy...? What! Is there a god besides Allah? Exalted is Allah above [having] any partners that they ascribe [to Him].\nاَمَّنْ يَّبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ وَمَنْ يَّرْزُقُكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(64)\nAMMAYN YABDAUL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOHU WA MAYN YARZOQOKUM MENAS SAMAAA-E WAL-ARZ, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, QUL HAATOO BURHAANAKUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nIs He who originates the creation, then He will bring it back, and who provides for you from the sky and the earth...? What! Is there a god besides Allah? Say, ‘Produce your evidence, if you are truthful.’\nقُلْ لَّا يَعْلَمُ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ الْغَيْبَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ‌ؕ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(65)\nQUL LAA YA’LAMO MAN FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZIL GHAYBA ILLAL LAAH, WA MAA YASHO’ROONA AYYAANA YUB-A’SOON.\nSay, ‘No one in the heavens or the earth knows the Unseen except Allah, and they are not aware when they will be resurrected.’\nبَلِ ادّٰرَكَ عِلْمُهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ‌ بَلْ هُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهَا  بَلْ هُمْ مِّنْهَا عَمُوْنَ‏(66)\nBALID DAARAKA I’LMOHUM FIL AAKHERAH, BAL HUM FEE SHAKKIM MINHAA, BAL HUM MINHAA A’MOON.\nDo they comprehend the knowledge of the Hereafter? No, they are in doubt about it. Indeed, they are blind to it.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا تُرٰبًا وَّاٰبَآؤُنَاۤ اَئِنَّا لَمُخْرَجُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO A-EZAA KUNNAA TORAABAWN WA AABAAA-ONAA A-INNAA LAMUKHRAJOON.\nThe faithless say, ‘What! When we and our fathers have become dust shall we be raised [from the dead]?\nلَقَدْ وُعِدْنَا هٰذَا نَحْنُ وَاٰبَآؤُنَا مِنْ قَبْلُۙ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(68)\nLAQAD WO-I’DNAA HAAZAA NAHNO WA AABAAA-ONAA MIN QABLO, IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nWe and our fathers were promised this before. [But] these are just myths of the ancients.’\nقُلْ سِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(69)\nQUL SEEROO FIL ARZE FANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUJREMEEN.\nSay, ‘Travel over the land and observe how was the fate of the guilty.’\nوَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا تَكُنْ فِىْ ضَيْقٍ مِّمَّا يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(70)\nWA LAA TAHZAN A’LAYHIM WA LAA TAKUN FEE ZAYQIM MIMMAA YAMKOROON.\nDo not grieve for them, and do not be upset by their guile.\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(71)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAL WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThey say, ‘When will this promise be fulfilled, if you are truthful?’\nقُلْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ رَدِفَ لَكُمْ بَعْضُ الَّذِىْ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(72)\nQUL A’SAA AYN YAKOONA RADEFA LAKUM BA’ZUL LAZEE TASTA’JELOON.\nSay, ‘Perhaps there is right behind you some of what you seek to hasten.’\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(73)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAZOO FAZLIN A’LAN NAASE WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YASHKOROON.\nIndeed your Lord is gracious to mankind, but most of them do not give thanks.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُكِنُّ صُدُوْرُهُمْ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(74)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LA-YA’LAMO MAA TOKINNO SODOOROHUM WA MAA YO’LENOON.\nYour Lord knows whatever their breasts conceal, and whatever they disclose.\nوَمَا مِنْ غَآئِبَةٍ فِى السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(75)\nWA MAA MIN GHAAA-EBATIN FIS SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nThere is no invisible thing in the heaven and the earth but it is in a manifest Book.\nاِنَّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ يَقُصُّ عَلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اَكْثَرَ الَّذِىْ هُمْ فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(76)\nINNA HAAZAL QURAANA YAQUSSO A’LAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA AKSARAL LAZEE HUM FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nThis Quran recounts for the Children of Israel most of what they differ about,\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(77)\nWA INNAHU LAHODAWN WA RAHMATUL LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nand it is indeed a guidance and mercy for the faithful.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِىْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِحُكْمِهٖ‌ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْعَلِيْمُ ۙ‌ۚ‏(78)\nINNA RABBAKA YAQZEE BAYNAHUM BEHUKMEH, WA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL A’LEEM.\nYour Lord will decide between them by His judgement, and He is the All-mighty, the All-knowing.\nفَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّكَ عَلَى الْحَقِّ الْمُبِيْنِ‏(79)\nFATAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAH, INNAKA A’LAL HAQQIL MOBEEN.\nSo put your trust in Allah, for you indeed stand on the manifest truth.\nاِنَّكَ لَا تُسْمِعُ الْمَوْتٰى وَلَا تُسْمِعُ الصُّمَّ الدُّعَآءَ اِذَا وَلَّوْا مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(80)\nINNAKA LAA TUSME-U’L MAWTAA WA LAA TUSME-U’S SUMMAD DO-A’AA-A EZAA WALLAW MUDBEREEN.\nYou cannot make the dead hear, nor can you make the deaf listen to your call when they turn their backs,\nوَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِهٰدِى الْعُمْىِ عَنْ ضَلٰلَتِهِمْ‌ؕ اِنْ تُسْمِعُ اِلَّا مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَهُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(81)\nWA MAA ANTA BEHAADIL U’MYE A’N ZALAALATEHIM, IN TUSME-O’ ILLAA MAYN YOAMENO BE-AAYAATENAA FAHUM MUSLEMOON.\nnor can you lead the blind out of their error. You can make only those hear you who believe in Our signs and have submitted.\nوَ اِذَا وَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ اَخْرَجْنَا لَهُمْ دَآبَّةً مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ تُكَلِّمُهُمْۙ اَنَّ النَّاسَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا لَا يُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(82)\nWA EZAA WAQA-A’L QAWLO A’LAYHIM AKHRAJNAA LAHUM DAAAB-BATAM MENAL ARZE TOKALLEMOHUM, ANNAN NAASA KAANOO BE-AAYAATENAA LAA YOOQENOON.\nWhen the word [of judgement] falls upon them, We shall bring out for them an Animal from the earth who shall tell them that the people had no faith in Our signs.\nوَ يَوْمَ نَحْشُرُ مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ فَوْجًا مِّمَّنْ يُّكَذِّبُ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَهُمْ يُوْزَعُوْنَ‏(83)\nWA YAWMA NAHSHORO MIN KULLE UMMATIN FAWJAM MIMMAYN YOKAZZEBO BE-AAYAATENAA FAHUM YOOZA-O’ON.\nOn that day We shall resurrect from every nation a group of those who denied Our signs, and they will be held in check.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءُوْ قَالَ اَكَذَّبْتُمْ بِاٰيٰتِىْ وَلَمْ تُحِيْطُوْا بِهَا عِلْمًا اَمَّاذَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(84)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-OO QAALA AKAZZABTUM BE-AAYAATEE WA LAM TOHEETOO BEHAA I’LMAA AMMAA ZAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nWhen they come, He will say, ‘Did you deny My signs without comprehending them in knowledge? What was it that you used to do?’\nوَوَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِمَا ظَلَمُوْا فَهُمْ لَا يَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA WAQA-A’L QAWLO A’LAYHIM BEMAA ZALAMOO FAHUM LAA YANTEQOON.\nAnd the word [of judgement] shall fall upon them for their wrongdoing, and they will not speak.\nاَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا جَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ لِيَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(86)\nALAM YARAW ANNAA JA-A’LNAL LAYLA LEYASKONOO FEEHE WAN NAHAARA MUBSERAA, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMIYN YOAMENOON.\nDo they not see that We made the night that they may rest in it, and the day to provide visibility. There are indeed signs in that for a people who have faith.\nوَيَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِىْ الصُّوْرِ فَفَزِعَ مَنْ فِىْ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا مَنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ‌ؕ وَكُلٌّ اَتَوْهُ دٰخِرِيْنَ‏(87)\nWA YAWMA YUNFAKHO FIS SOORE FA-FAZE-A’ MAN FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZE ILLAAMAN SHAAA-AL LAAH, WA KULLUN ATAWHO DAAKHEREEN.\nThe day when the trumpet is blown, whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will be terrified, except such as Allah wishes, and all will come to Him in utter humility.\nوَتَرَى الْجِبَالَ تَحْسَبُهَا جَامِدَةً وَّهِىَ تَمُرُّ مَرَّ السَّحَابِ‌ؕ صُنْعَ اللّٰهِ الَّذِىْۤ اَتْقَنَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(88)\nWA TARAL JEBAALA TAHSABOHAA JAAMEDATAWN WA HEYA TAMURRO MARRAS SAHAAB, SUN-A’L LAAHIL LAZEE ATQANA KULLA SHAY-IN, INNAHU KHABEERUM BEMAA TAF-A’LOON.\nYou see the mountains, which you suppose, to be stationary, while they drift like passing clouds—the handiwork of Allah who has made everything faultless. He is indeed well aware of what you do.\nمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهٗ خَيْرٌ مِّنْهَا‌ۚ وَهُمْ مِّنْ فَزَعٍ يَّوْمَئِذٍ اٰمِنُوْنَ‏(89)\nMAN JAAA-A BIL-HASANATE FALAHU KHARUM MINHAA, WA HUM MIN FAZA-I’YN YAWMA-EZIN AAMENOON.\nWhoever brings virtue shall receive [a reward] better than it; and on that day they will be secure from terror.\nوَمَنْ جَآءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَكُبَّتْ وُجُوْهُهُمْ فِى النَّارِؕ هَلْ تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(90)\nWA MAN JAAA-A BIS-SAYYE-ATE FAKUBBAT WOJOOHOHUM FIN NAAR, HAL TUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nBut whoever brings vice—they shall be cast on their faces into the Fire [and told:] ‘Shall you not be requited for what you used to do?’\nاِنَّمَاۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ رَبَّ هٰذِهِ الْبَلْدَةِ الَّذِىْ حَرَّمَهَا وَلَهٗ كُلُّ شَىْءٍ‌ وَّاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَۙ‏(91)\nINNAMAA UMIRTO AN A-A’BODA RABBA HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEE HARRAMAHAA WA LAHU KULLO SHAYIWN, WA UMIRTO AN A-A’BODA RABBA HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEE HARRAMAHAA WA LAHU KULLO SHAY-IWN, WA UMIRTO AN AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\n[Say], ‘I have been commanded to worship the Lord of this city who has made it inviolable and to whom all things belong, and I have been commanded to be among those who submit [to Allah],\nوَاَنْ اَتْلُوَا الْقُرْاٰنَ‌ۚ فَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِىْ لِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُنْذِرِيْنَ‏(92)\nWA AN ATLOWAL QURAAN, FAMANEH TADAA FA-INNAMAA YAHTADEE LENAFSEH, WA MAN ZALLA FAQUL INNAMAA ANAA MENAL MUNZEREEN.\nand to recite the Quran.’ Whoever is guided is guided only for his own good, and as for him who goes astray, say, ‘I am just one of the warners.’\nوَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ سَيُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ فَتَعْرِفُوْنَهَا‌ ؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHE SAYOREEKUM AAYAATEHI FA-TA’REFOONAHAA, WA MAA RABBOKA BEGHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nAnd say, ‘All praise belongs to Allah. Soon He will show you His signs, and you will recognize them.’ Your Lord is not oblivious of what you do.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Naml (The Ant)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 93 verses. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan, it is written that the reward for reciting this Surah is compared to ten times the number of people alive during the time of Prophets Sulaiman (a.s.), Hud (a.s.), Shoa’ib (a.s.), Saaleh (a.s.) and Ibrahim (a.s.).\nIn the commentary of Burhan it is written that if this Surah is written on deerskin and kept in the house, then no dangerous creature (e.g. snake) will come near the house. This has been narrated by Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.)."
